two cases are currently supported by the code 1) twophase with gravity on the ELEMENT 2) singlephase with gravity on the ELEMENT_INTEGRATION_POINT

.PP
projection of a vector g(0,-1,0) onto a vector r(r[0],r[1],r[2]) (where |r|=1) is equal to (r, g)r = -r[1] r

.PP
r*=(r[1]>0\&.0?-1:1) Note that the direction of the gravity force should be oriented downwards

.PP
projection of vector g(0,-1, 0) onto a surface with a normal vector n(n[0], n[1], n[2]) (where |n|=1) is equal to n x (n x g) = (n, g) n - g = -n[1] n - g 
.br

.PP
n*=(n[1]>0\&.0?-1:1) Note that the direction of the gravity force should be oriented downwards
